WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.527
Week 21: Direct and Indirect Objects. track who receives what avoid unnecessary repetition clarify a transaction

2
00:00:08.527 --> 00:00:14.815
Cultural lens. Gift giving, favors, reciprocity, and degrees of explicitness.

3
00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:26.886
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:26.886 --> 00:00:38.744
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:47.743
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:47.743 --> 00:01:19.100
Model language. Un regalo no siempre espera reciprocidad. — A gift doesn't always expect reciprocity. Un favor puede ser explícito o implícito. — A favor can be explicit or implicit. Es común agradecer un favor recibido. — It's common to thank a favor received. Corresponder no siempre es obligatorio. — Reciprocating isn't always required. Cada cultura tiene su propia expectativa. — Each culture has its own expectation.

7
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:29.019
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
